{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AbGfJjDqBGTVf1TazLu34a","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've found comprehensive information about experiment plans and tier definitions. Let me compile my findings.\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\nI found an extensive set of YAML and markdown files related to experiment plans and tier definitions in the project. Here are the key files:\n\n### Main Experiment Plan File\n**File:** `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/experiment_plan.yaml`\n\nThis is the primary experiment planning document containing 17 experiments (exp-001 through exp-017) organized with:\n- Experiment IDs, names, descriptions, priorities (P0/P1/P2)\n- GPU budget hours and dependencies\n- Registry IDs and detailed notes\n- Focus on NER (Named Entity Recognition) and RE (Relation Extraction) tasks\n\nKey experiments include:\n- exp-001: NER N=16 on SciERC with multiple seeds\n- exp-002/003: Cross-dataset NER on CoNLL-2003 and WNUT-17\n- exp-012-015: Baseline comparisons (log-prob, exact-match, entity-voting, metrics expansion)\n- exp-006-010: Best-of-N selection, model validation, selection curves\n\n### Dream Registry and Tier Definitions\n**Files:** \n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/dream_registry.yaml`\n- Dream report YAML files in `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/`\n\nThe dream_registry.yaml contains 3 dream scenarios with different tiers:\n\n1. **dream_20260514T093336** (best tier):\n   - Status: done\n   - Focus: NER-primary paper with RE diagnostic\n\n2. **dream_20260514T105303** (median tier):\n   - Status: done\n   - Focus: Post-revision dream comparing 4 confidence signal families\n   - Reframed contribution as systematic comparison\n\n3. **dream_20260514T203201** (worst tier):\n   - Status: imagining\n   - Focus: All GPU experiments completed, 5-signal comparison framework\n   - Written in Chinese/mixed language\n\n### Imagined Experiments by Tier\n\nEach dream contains detailed **imagined_experiments** YAML files defining expected results and analysis:\n\n**Best Tier** (`/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T105303/best/imagined_experiments.yaml`):\n- SJ (Soft Jaccard) significantly outperforms log-prob across all metrics\n- Δρ ≥ 0.12 demonstrates structural consistency value\n- 16x inference cost justified by best-of-N F1 improvements (+4.5pp)\n\n**Median Tier** (`/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T105303/median/imagined_experiments.yaml`):\n- SJ and log-prob are complementary rather than competitive\n- Log-prob is stronger than expected (ρ=0.34)\n- Contribution reframed as systematic comparison of 4 signal families\n- SJ+logprob ensemble achieves ρ=0.42-0.44\n\n**Worst Tier** (`/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T105303/worst/imagined_experiments.yaml`):\n- Log-prob matches or exceeds SJ on NER\n- All confidence signals degrade on RE (task-complexity boundary)\n- SJ exhibits ceiling effect on easy datasets (CoNLL) and floor effect on hard datasets (WNUT)\n- Contribution reframed as systematic negative result + diagnostic framework\n\n### Key Files Summary\n\n| File Path | Purpose |\n|-----------|---------|\n| `experiment_plan.yaml` | Master experiment specification |\n| `dream_registry.yaml` | Dream scenario metadata |\n| `dream_*/best/imagined_experiments.yaml` | Best-case scenario with detailed expected results |\n| `dream_*/median/imagined_experiments.yaml` | Middle-ground scenario with more nuanced findings |\n| `dream_*/worst/imagined_experiments.yaml` | Worst-case scenario with negative/challenging results |\n| `dream_*/*/paper_framing.md` | Narrative guidance for each tier |\n| `dream_*/*/review_context.yaml` | Review-specific context |\n\nAll imagined experiments include detailed result tables, figures descriptions, rationales, and analysis sections organized by multiple metric types (ρ, AUROC, τ, ECE, etc.)."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"be60cc2d-21a9-4d86-8473-16b9efb6edfb","uuid":"33133698-ceb8-446d-9455-dec6e4e09f3c","timestamp":"2026-05-14T20:51:21.867Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Search for any YAML or markdown files related to experiment plans, tier definitions, or worst-case scenario definitions in the project directory /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1. Look for files like experiment_plan.yaml, tiers.yaml, worst_tier.yaml, or similar. Also check for any existing imagined_experiments files. Search breadth: medium.","agentId":"a91113e72c97570bf","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've found comprehensive information about experiment plans and tier definitions. Let me compile my findings.\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\nI found an extensive set of YAML and markdown files related to experiment plans and tier definitions in the project. Here are the key files:\n\n### Main Experiment Plan File\n**File:** `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/experiment_plan.yaml`\n\nThis is the primary experiment planning document containing 17 experiments (exp-001 through exp-017) organized with:\n- Experiment IDs, names, descriptions, priorities (P0/P1/P2)\n- GPU budget hours and dependencies\n- Registry IDs and detailed notes\n- Focus on NER (Named Entity Recognition) and RE (Relation Extraction) tasks\n\nKey experiments include:\n- exp-001: NER N=16 on SciERC with multiple seeds\n- exp-002/003: Cross-dataset NER on CoNLL-2003 and WNUT-17\n- exp-012-015: Baseline comparisons (log-prob, exact-match, entity-voting, metrics expansion)\n- exp-006-010: Best-of-N selection, model validation, selection curves\n\n### Dream Registry and Tier Definitions\n**Files:** \n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/dream_registry.yaml`\n- Dream report YAML files in `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/`\n\nThe dream_registry.yaml contains 3 dream scenarios with different tiers:\n\n1. **dream_20260514T093336** (best tier):\n   - Status: done\n   - Focus: NER-primary paper with RE diagnostic\n\n2. **dream_20260514T105303** (median tier):\n   - Status: done\n   - Focus: Post-revision dream comparing 4 confidence signal families\n   - Reframed contribution as systematic comparison\n\n3. **dream_20260514T203201** (worst tier):\n   - Status: imagining\n   - Focus: All GPU experiments completed, 5-signal comparison framework\n   - Written in Chinese/mixed language\n\n### Imagined Experiments by Tier\n\nEach dream contains detailed **imagined_experiments** YAML files defining expected results and analysis:\n\n**Best Tier** (`/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T105303/best/imagined_experiments.yaml`):\n- SJ (Soft Jaccard) significantly outperforms log-prob across all metrics\n- Δρ ≥ 0.12 demonstrates structural consistency value\n- 16x inference cost justified by best-of-N F1 improvements (+4.5pp)\n\n**Median Tier** (`/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T105303/median/imagined_experiments.yaml`):\n- SJ and log-prob are complementary rather than competitive\n- Log-prob is stronger than expected (ρ=0.34)\n- Contribution reframed as systematic comparison of 4 signal families\n- SJ+logprob ensemble achieves ρ=0.42-0.44\n\n**Worst Tier** (`/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T105303/worst/imagined_experiments.yaml`):\n- Log-prob matches or exceeds SJ on NER\n- All confidence signals degrade on RE (task-complexity boundary)\n- SJ exhibits ceiling effect on easy datasets (CoNLL) and floor effect on hard datasets (WNUT)\n- Contribution reframed as systematic negative result + diagnostic framework\n\n### Key Files Summary\n\n| File Path | Purpose |\n|-----------|---------|\n| `experiment_plan.yaml` | Master experiment specification |\n| `dream_registry.yaml` | Dream scenario metadata |\n| `dream_*/best/imagined_experiments.yaml` | Best-case scenario with detailed expected results |\n| `dream_*/median/imagined_experiments.yaml` | Middle-ground scenario with more nuanced findings |\n| `dream_*/worst/imagined_experiments.yaml` | Worst-case scenario with negative/challenging results |\n| `dream_*/*/paper_framing.md` | Narrative guidance for each tier |\n| `dream_*/*/review_context.yaml` | Review-specific context |\n\nAll imagined experiments include detailed result tables, figures descriptions, rationales, and analysis sections organized by multiple metric types (ρ, AUROC, τ, ECE, etc.)."}],"totalDurationMs":21185,"totalTokens":97819,"totalToolUseCount":9,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":77614,"cache_read_input_tokens":19090,"output_tokens":1108,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":77614},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":7,"output_tokens":1108,"cache_read_input_tokens":19090,"cache_creation_input_tokens":77614,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":77614,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":5,"searchCount":4,"bashCount":0,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
